    {
      "name": "Entry Row",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "hero-ledger-panel",
      "description": "Visitors-book entry: Bitter date numeral and gilt stamp in the left column, ruled above and below.",
      "html": "<ul class=\"ds-entries\"><li class=\"ds-entry\"><div class=\"ds-date\"><span class=\"ds-day\">14</span><span class=\"ds-stamp2\">Dec · 10:00</span></div><div><p class=\"ds-etitle\">Carol service and fellowship lunch</p><p class=\"ds-emeta\">Main auditorium</p></div></li><li class=\"ds-entry\"><div class=\"ds-date\"><span class=\"ds-day\">21</span><span class=\"ds-stamp2\">Dec · 09:00</span></div><div><p class=\"ds-etitle\">Bible class for new members</p><p class=\"ds-emeta\">Fellowship hall</p></div></li></ul>",
      "css": ":host{--c-surface:#fff;--c-surface-muted:#f5f7fa;--c-surface-sunken:#ebeff5;--c-rule:#d5deea;--c-rule-strong:#b4c3d6;--c-margin:#c0392b;--c-ink:#172131;--c-ink-muted:#4b5768;--c-ink-subtle:#5f6b7c;--c-primary:#1e4d3b;--c-primary-hover:#163b2d;--c-primary-active:#10301f;--c-primary-soft:#e6efea;--c-on-primary:#fff;--c-secondary:#24364f;--c-accent:#8a5d0f;--c-accent-soft:#f6eedd;--c-success:#1f7a45;--c-success-soft:#e5f3ea;--c-error:#b42318;--c-error-soft:#fdecea;--c-focus:#1f5fa8;}.ds-entries{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0;border-top:1px solid var(--c-rule-strong);border-bottom:1px solid var(--c-rule-strong);font-family:'Public Sans',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-entry{display:flex;gap:24px;align-items:center;padding:24px 0;}.ds-entry+.ds-entry{border-top:1px solid var(--c-rule);}.ds-date{display:flex;flex-direction:column;width:80px;flex-shrink:0;}.ds-day{font-family:Bitter,'Roboto Slab',Rockwell,Georgia,serif;font-size:36px;line-height:1;font-weight:700;color:var(--c-secondary);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums lining-nums;}.ds-stamp2{margin-top:6px;font-size:12px;line-height:16px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:0.06em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--c-accent);}.ds-etitle{margin:0;font-family:Bitter,'Roboto Slab',Rockwell,Georgia,serif;font-size:20px;line-height:1.375;font-weight:600;color:var(--c-ink);}.ds-emeta{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:16px;color:var(--c-ink-muted);}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Tabs",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "tab-active",
      "description": "Ruled tab row with a bookcloth underline on the active tab.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-tabs\" role=\"tablist\"><button class=\"ds-tab\" aria-selected=\"true\">Members</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Visitors</button><button class=\"ds-tab\">Children</button></div>",
      "css": ":host{--c-surface:#fff;--c-surface-muted:#f5f7fa;--c-surface-sunken:#ebeff5;--c-rule:#d5deea;--c-rule-strong:#b4c3d6;--c-margin:#c0392b;--c-ink:#172131;--c-ink-muted:#4b5768;--c-ink-subtle:#5f6b7c;--c-primary:#1e4d3b;--c-primary-hover:#163b2d;--c-primary-active:#10301f;--c-primary-soft:#e6efea;--c-on-primary:#fff;--c-secondary:#24364f;--c-accent:#8a5d0f;--c-accent-soft:#f6eedd;--c-success:#1f7a45;--c-success-soft:#e5f3ea;--c-error:#b42318;--c-error-soft:#fdecea;--c-focus:#1f5fa8;}.ds-tabs{display:flex;gap:4px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--c-rule);font-family:'Public Sans',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-tab{margin-bottom:-1px;min-height:44px;padding:0 14px;border:none;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;background:none;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;color:var(--c-ink-muted);cursor:pointer;transition:color 150ms,border-color 150ms;}.ds-tab:hover{border-bottom-color:var(--c-rule-strong);color:var(--c-ink);}.ds-tab[aria-selected=\"true\"]{border-bottom-color:var(--c-primary);font-weight:600;color:var(--c-primary);}.ds-tab:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--c-focus);outline-offset:2px;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Admin Sidebar Item",
      "kind": "nav",
      "refersTo": "sidebar-item-active",
      "description": "Bookcloth spine navigation with a white active tile.",
      "html": "<nav class=\"ds-side\"><a class=\"ds-side-item is-active\" href=\"#\"><svg width=\"19\" height=\"19\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M19 3h-1V1h-2v2H8V1H6v2H5a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v14a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h14a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V5a2 2 0 0 0-2-2m0 16H5V8h14zm-9.4-2.3-3.5-3.5 1.4-1.4 2.1 2.1 4.8-4.8 1.4 1.4z\"/></svg>Attendance</a><a class=\"ds-side-item\" href=\"#\"><svg width=\"19\" height=\"19\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\"><path d=\"M20 4H4a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v12a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h16a2 2 0 0 0 2-2V6a2 2 0 0 0-2-2m0 14H4V8l8 5 8-5zm-8-7L4 6h16z\"/></svg>Messages<span class=\"ds-count\">3</span></a></nav>",
      "css": ":host{--c-surface:#fff;--c-surface-muted:#f5f7fa;--c-surface-sunken:#ebeff5;--c-rule:#d5deea;--c-rule-strong:#b4c3d6;--c-margin:#c0392b;--c-ink:#172131;--c-ink-muted:#4b5768;--c-ink-subtle:#5f6b7c;--c-primary:#1e4d3b;--c-primary-hover:#163b2d;--c-primary-active:#10301f;--c-primary-soft:#e6efea;--c-on-primary:#fff;--c-secondary:#24364f;--c-accent:#8a5d0f;--c-accent-soft:#f6eedd;--c-success:#1f7a45;--c-success-soft:#e5f3ea;--c-error:#b42318;--c-error-soft:#fdecea;--c-focus:#1f5fa8;}.ds-side{width:240px;padding:16px 12px;background-color:var(--c-primary);display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;font-family:'Public Sans',ui-sans-serif,system-ui,sans-serif;}.ds-side-item{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;min-height:40px;padding:0 12px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;color:rgb(255 255 255 / 0.8);text-decoration:none;transition:background-color 150ms,color 150ms;}.ds-side-item svg{color:rgb(255 255 255 / 0.6);}.ds-side-item:hover{background:rgb(255 255 255 / 0.1);color:#fff;}.ds-side-item.is-active{background:#fff;color:var(--c-primary-hover);box-shadow:0 1px 2px rgb(23 33 49 / 0.06),0 1px 3px rgb(23 33 49 / 0.08);}.ds-side-item.is-active svg{color:var(--c-primary);}.ds-side-item:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #f2c14e;outline-offset:2px;}.ds-count{margin-left:auto;min-width:24px;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;background:#f2d593;color:#3b2a06;font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-align:center;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Register",
    "overview": "Congregation is the church's record books made legible. The public site is the visitors' book at the door; the admin dashboard is the registers themselves: the nominal roll, the attendance book, the collections ledger. Everything is built from the materials of a bound record book: white ledger pages laid on a cool rule-blue ground, feint blue rules between entries, a red double margin down the left of a page heading, a deep green bookcloth binding, blue-black ink, and small gilt stamps for dates and categories.\n\nDensity follows the audience. Public pages are generous and legible for first-time visitors and older congregants on phones: 16-18px body, 44-48px touch targets, 64-96px section rhythm, entries set as ruled rows with a big slab date in the margin. Admin pages are a working register: 14px body, ruled data tables with sticky headers, tabular figures in every column, white panels on the canvas ground, one bookcloth spine on the left. Both surfaces are light only; there is no dark mode.\n\nThe system rejects the church-template look (a stock photo hero over three icon cards) and the grey SaaS dashboard. Depth is quiet (hairline rules first, soft ink-tinted shadows second), corners are squared like a bound book, and colour is committed rather than decorative: bookcloth green is the one field colour, everything else is ink on paper.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White ledger panels on a rule-blue canvas; feint blue hairlines as the default divider.",
      "One structural signature: the red double margin, on headers and a single featured entry only.",
      "Bookcloth green carries the nav band, footer, admin sidebar, and every primary action.",
      "Bitter slab for headings and figures, Public Sans for everything read.",
      "Tabular lining figures wherever a number appears.",
      "Squared corners (6-8px), hairline borders, soft low shadows; no glows, no glass, no pills except avatars and status dots.",
      "Light mode only, everywhere. No dark mode."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Binding Rule",
        "body": "Bookcloth green is the only colour that fills large areas. Every other hue appears as text, a hairline, a dot, or a soft tint.",
